    "methods": {
      "generators": "Two Apache-2.0 families, one offline affine Q4 MLX attempt each on every fixed target. Existing complete-response, word bounds and source-copy gates. Fixed format/word-count recovery only, no detector-based selection.",
      "human_controls": "Original, exact same-source paragraph substitution and one complete sentence substitution.",
      "isolated": "The same single eligible paragraph must also reach .5 with an independent forward on the isolated paragraph. The weights are the same as current and responses are correlated.",
      "metric": "Flagged human source groups and human files, plus non-whitespace IoU >= .30 for eligible rewrites, including paired current transitions and false alarms before fitting. No new point fit or serving change.",
      "omission": "Also require the three-paragraph raw response to exceed the response with the current paragraph omitted, and removing the current paragraph must give a strictly lower response than either matched two-paragraph input formed by omitting one neighbor. The test also changes length, content, topic and transitions. It is a measured response perturbation with shared weights, not authorship probability.",
      "paragraph": "Each interior paragraph needs a navigation focus with current raw >= .5. Choose the highest raw supporting focus, break ties by earliest source, and mark only the chosen entire paragraph.",
      "raw": "Same current native classifier inputs and first six qualifying foci, score >= .5. Include consumed practical .85 and archived strict and pooled rules unchanged.",
      "wide": "Also require >= .5 on the contiguous previous + current + next paragraph input."
    },
